dot-edit(1) -- Edit or view a dotfile, respecting your chosen $EDITOR by default
==================================================================================

## SYNOPSIS

`dot edit` [-h] [-cvnl] [<file>]

## DESCRIPTION

Edit or view a dotfile, respecting the your chosen editor (set in $EDITOR) by default.

<!-- This subcommand is especially helpful for scripting and is actually used by **dot**'s Zsh completions (via `dotmgr.dot.DynamicChoices` and compmaker.py) to dynamically determine the available choices within the completion itself. -->

Part of dot(1).

## OPTIONS

  * `-h`, `--h`:
    Show command help.

  * [<file>]:
    Relative path of the managed dotfile (optional). If no file is given, the dotfiles repository will be opened instead.

  * `-c`:
    Open the file in Visual Studio Code

  * `-v`:
    Open the file in Vim

  * `-n`:
    Open the file in Nano
  
  * `-l`:
    Open the file in Less
